				<title>SCP-5913</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5913</link>
				<description>


&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: right;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Item#:&lt;/strong&gt; 5913&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Object Class:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: line-through;&quot;&gt;Euclid&lt;/span&gt; Keter&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Special Containment Procedures:&lt;/strong&gt; Containment of SCP-5913 is a 16 x 60 ft (about 3.7 x 5.5m) room constructed out of tungsten. The subject is to keep under the observer of the foundation surveillances at all times. All personnel is to test for cognitohazardous corruption before they entered its containment cell. It was advised all personnel of the Foundation not to make any physical interactions with the subject.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Description&lt;/strong&gt;: SCP-5913 is a humanoid entity dressed up in a bartender suit of the 1920s,&lt;sup class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;&gt;&lt;a id=&quot;footnoteref-898321-1&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot; class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;  &gt;1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt; This may be either real cloth or some form of skin molded to take on cloth&#039;s appearance. Subject measures 6 to 15 feet tall have a general appearance as a tall black figure. Its face is pitch black, utterly devoid of facial features.&lt;sup class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;&gt;&lt;a id=&quot;footnoteref-898321-2&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot; class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;  &gt;2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The subject has no sign of hair, eyes, nose, and mouth can be opened up as an average human and has normal-looking bare hands, albeit with fingers longer and bonier than a typical human 1.5 meters each. However, it is possible that this is not SCP-5913&#039;s proper form and that it is an eldritch being that cannot comprehend whose proper form. It can speak and understand common human languages; however, the subject seems to have different respiratory sounds, which causes it to have issues in saying.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Attempting to kill SCP-5913 often has some significant problems because of its considerable physical and uncommon abilities. It has always been observed to have chief strength, speed, and reflexes. The documented rate has varied; it can run with speed up to Mach 25; however, sometimes, the subject prefers to teleport rather than running.&lt;sup class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;&gt;&lt;a id=&quot;footnoteref-898321-3&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot; class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;  &gt;3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt; Other than that, the subject is not sustainable. However, SCP-5913 has shown to have a remarkable ability to ignore pain, shock, and a decisive regenerate healing factor.&lt;sup class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;&gt;&lt;a id=&quot;footnoteref-898321-4&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot; class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;  &gt;4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The tendrils that sprout from SCP-5913&#039;s body can grab and attack; it can also use the tendrils as a shield to protect the entity away from harm.&lt;sup class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;&gt;&lt;a id=&quot;footnoteref-898321-5&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot; class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;  &gt;5&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Its presence causes several adverse effects on the minds of its targets, including inhibiting memory loss, adding memory, altering sense and perception of a person&#039;s environment, influencing a person&#039;s personality in a very negative way such as causing a great deal of paranoia, nightmares, and hallucinations, Etc. It is believed that the presence of SCP-5913 directly causes adverse effects on the minds of whom it manifest. There is evidence that supports this belief. People who encounter it would become incredibly paranoid of its next return, easily irritated or agitated, severely depressed, and sometimes even suicidal. This method of negatively changing a person&#039;s personality could most likely result from its mind control.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Documents of SCP-5913 anomalous abilities have shown particular individual contemporary views see its movement unlimited as if it can move its body properly. There is no apparent coherency to its positions. It can teleport several dozen times to various locations in a few seconds. SCP-5913 does not flee and can be just as dangerous standing still as when teleporting. It is capable of – and often will – stay within several dozen feet of its target, no matter how they try to escape. It seems to be part of SCP-5913&#039;s psychological ways of attacking to stay just within visual range without attacking — the fact that it is there, no matter what, it described worse than being attacked, the psychological effects often deteriorating the minds of its targets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SCP-5913 appears to follow all targets regardless of where they go or where and how they hide. It is not sure how it does this, but it seems to keep a perfect trace on its targets. These accounts vary from person to person, but being an SCP-5913 target is almost contagious or memetic. One can become its victim by encountering someone it is already targeting. Primary research and even collecting information does not appear to incur its notice. A theory sprouts from this, discussing how it could track several people at once due to the apparent number of people invested. This theory states he is an omnipresent being.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Its skin can inflict diseases upon those who touch it; humans who come in contact with SCP-5913&#039;s skin would cause them to suffer some common ailments.&lt;sup class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;&gt;&lt;a id=&quot;footnoteref-898321-6&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot; class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;  &gt;6&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Addendum 5913.1: Discovery&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In the mid-1900s, at the South East of America, the Foundation has written that following witness reports of something lurking inside a large abandoned row home located somewhere deep in the forest. These reports resulted in the dispatching of Mobile Task Force Omega-7, who arrived on site with 15 armed personnel. During capturing SCP-5913, seven (7) personnel were lost in action; however, later on, one of the agents had weakened a while later. After that, it got transported back to Site-19. However, due to having issues occur while traveling back, Omega-7 was ordered by the Foundation to transport SCP-5913 to Site-179, where it was contained in a reinforced 14m x 14m x 14m room made out of alloy steel. Armed guards are to be in place at all times to prevent unauthorized access to the facility. One of the foundation researchers, Dr.█████, interviewed it to see whether he can find anything to learn about SCP-5913.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre-wrap;&quot;&gt;&amp;#32;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;background: url(http://kaktuskontainer.wdfiles.com/local--files/format-hell/scp_trans.png) center no-repeat ; float: center; border: solid 2px #000000; padding: 1px 15px; box-shadow: 0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,.2);&quot;&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span&gt;WARNING: THE FOLLOWING FILES ARE LEVEL 4/5913 CLASSIFIED&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span&gt;THE FOLLOWING FILES CONTAIN REFERENCES TO PROCEDURES RETROACTIVELY DECLARED BY THE ETHICS COMMITTEE TO BE RECKLESSLY NEGLIGENT. ANY FURTHER ATTEMPTS TO ACCESS MATERIALS RELATED TO THESE PROCEDURES WITHOUT PROPER CLEARANCE WILL LEAD TO IMMEDIATE DISCIPLINARY ACTION.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre-wrap;&quot;&gt;&amp;#32;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Addendum XXXX.1A: Interview and Experiment Logs&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-folded&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;collapsible-block-link&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;SCP-5913-1A:&amp;nbsp;Interview&amp;nbsp;Log&amp;nbsp;(10/10/1935)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-unfolded&quot; style=&quot;display:none&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-unfolded-link&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;collapsible-block-link&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;ACCESS&amp;nbsp;GRANTED&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-content&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Addendum 5913-1A Interview Log:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;display: inline-block; border-radius: 10px; border:dashed 1px #444444; background:#F5F5F5; float:top; width:96.5%; padding:10px&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;[BEGIN LOG]&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;(SCP-5913 growls in an aggressive tone)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5913:&lt;/strong&gt; Where am I?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr.█████:&lt;/strong&gt; Calm down. We do not mean any harm to any at all.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;(Silence)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5913:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;#8230;Who&amp;#8230;are you? Furthermore, what do you want with me?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr.█████&lt;/strong&gt; Yes, allow me to introduce myself; my Name is Dr.█████, and what I want is for you to answer some questions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5913:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;#8230;What questions?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr.█████:&lt;/strong&gt; It is nothing serious at all, I need to ask you a few simple questions, and that is all.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5913:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;(Silence)&lt;/em&gt; Okay, I’m listening.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr.█████:&lt;/strong&gt; So, first, may I know your name?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5913:&lt;/strong&gt; Name? I do not have a name.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr.█████:&lt;/strong&gt; Is that so? In that case, would you mind if I refer to you as SCP-5913?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5913:&lt;/strong&gt; Well&amp;#8230;if that is what you want to call me then, all right.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr.█████:&lt;/strong&gt; Okay, so, what date were you born?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5913:&lt;/strong&gt; I also have no clue of what day, month, and the year I was born in.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr.█████:&lt;/strong&gt; Okay, but I am still confused; earlier, we have sent a group of agents to come to your location. You have killed 7 of our agents before being weakened by the rest. If you can talk, then why didn&#039;t you tried to speak to field agents?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5913:&lt;/strong&gt; I thought they would not listen and would only kill me, so I have to fight back. I swear I do not want to kill or hurt anyone at all; it was just self-defense &lt;em&gt;(sighs)&lt;/em&gt; I should have just teleported away.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr.█████:&lt;/strong&gt; Wait, did you say you can teleport?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5913:&lt;/strong&gt; Yes, but I thought that if I let them live, they would lead back more and more &amp;quot;agents&amp;quot; to where I am from, and as I said from earlier, it was just self-defense. I did not want to die; that is all.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr.█████:&lt;/strong&gt; all right, then how long have you been inside that abandoned row home?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5913:&lt;/strong&gt; To be honest, I cannot even possibly remember how long has I been in there, probably years perhaps&amp;#8230;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr.█████:&lt;/strong&gt; I see, however, if you cannot remember, or maybe do not have a name, and the date that you were born in, even how long you have been in that abandoned row home, then were you human once?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5913:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;(Silence)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr.█████:&lt;/strong&gt; Uh, is everything all right?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5913:&lt;/strong&gt; Well, I do not recall any memories I have, but I still keep a few memories of my past-life before becoming like this.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr.█████:&lt;/strong&gt; So you were once human, huh?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5913:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;(Nods)&lt;/em&gt; Yes&amp;#8230;however, I do not have the memories of my past-self, except for a little that I can still remember.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr.█████:&lt;/strong&gt; Is that so?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5913:&lt;/strong&gt; Yeah&amp;#8230;I-I can remember working as a bartender during the mid-1900s.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr.█████:&lt;/strong&gt; Other than that, do you recall any other things else than your former job?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5913:&lt;/strong&gt; No, I think that is all I could remember…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr.█████:&lt;/strong&gt; I see, so how do you feel now?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5913:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;(Silence)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr.█████:&lt;/strong&gt; Um, excuse me, SCP-5913, are you listening?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5913:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;(Silence)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr.█████:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-XXXX, are you there?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5913:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;(Silence)&lt;/em&gt; Oh! S-sorry about that, I was just being distracted, so what were you saying?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr.█████:&lt;/strong&gt; Distracted? What exactly were you being distracted from?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5913:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;(Silence)&lt;/em&gt; Is that even neccessary?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr.█████:&lt;/strong&gt; Yes, it is. Everything related to you is necessary for the Foundation. So tell me, what were you being distracted from?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5913:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;(Sighs)&lt;/em&gt; Well, I kind of sense vital energy flowing around this entire so-called &amp;quot;facility&amp;quot; it is compelling if you asked.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr.█████:&lt;/strong&gt; What kind of compelling energy did you sense?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5913:&lt;/strong&gt; I do not know, but it makes me feel a bit of distress. This energy would be malevolence if you asked.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr.█████:&lt;/strong&gt; I see, so where does this &amp;quot;malevolence&amp;quot; energy do you sense is coming from?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5913:&lt;/strong&gt; Well, I believed it is somewhere around this facility.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr.█████:&lt;/strong&gt; I see. Is it possible that you were mentioning SCP-████&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5913:&lt;/strong&gt;, Huh? Who is that?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr.█████:&lt;/strong&gt; Not important.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5913:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;(Silence)&lt;/em&gt; Okay, but may I know why am I here in this place?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr.█████&lt;/strong&gt; Well, to be fair, a few issues have occurred with one of our vehicles.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5913:&lt;/strong&gt; Oh, so it did work while I was still resting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr.█████:&lt;/strong&gt; Excuse me?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5913:&lt;/strong&gt; Well, moments ago, while I was resting inside the container to regain my strength, I think one of my powers must have caused some technological problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr.█████:&lt;/strong&gt; Wait, so you tell me that you can cause out statics upon technology?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5913:&lt;/strong&gt; To be fair, I would prefer to call it a technological disruption. I had discovered that I could do so a few days earlier when I passed by a campsite, but I did not seem to get the hang of it yet heh.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr.█████:&lt;/strong&gt; Wait, I am confused. How calm you used your anomalous abilities while resting?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5913:&lt;/strong&gt; You see here, my technological disruption does not work the way it was. It happens naturally, anywhere I go, it happens without I want it to.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr.█████:&lt;/strong&gt; So you cannot control your powers, huh?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5913:&lt;/strong&gt; Yes, however, this power happens in random moments; it does not always happen, so I cannot tell when it will start to occur.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr.█████:&lt;/strong&gt; Uh-huh, other than that, is there anything else that you want to share with me?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5913:&lt;/strong&gt; Well, so, am I going to be here, or what?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr.█████:&lt;/strong&gt; You were supposed to be transported to a site that is far away from here. However, due to your powers interrupting the vehicle&#039;s control system, the Foundation has given out a new command was to temporarily transport you to this site until we received a new order from the Foundation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5913:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;(Silence)&lt;/em&gt; Which is?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr.█████:&lt;/strong&gt; Well, of course, it is the order of the Foundation to transport you back to the site where you were supposed to be transferred to.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5913:&lt;/strong&gt; I see; thanks for informing me that.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr.█████:&lt;/strong&gt; Okay, so how are you?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5913:&lt;/strong&gt; Excuse me? I did not quite get that. Can you be more specific about what you said just now?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr.█████:&lt;/strong&gt; What is your impression of your time in the Foundation so far?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5913:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;(Silence)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr.█████:&lt;/strong&gt; It is okay, to be honest. We do not take any offense at these things.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5913:&lt;/strong&gt; Well, this place&amp;#8230;the so-called &amp;quot;foundation&amp;quot; seems to be like some prison or, to be specific, it is like a prison for peoples like me if I am not wrong. However, I know it is better than getting myself killed. However, I am also curious about what will happen to me after being transported to the other so-called &amp;quot;site&amp;quot;?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr.█████:&lt;/strong&gt; Depends on the decisions of the Foundation, they will decide what to do with you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5913:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;(Silence)&lt;/em&gt; Okay, I get it&amp;#8230;thanks for telling me this.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr.█████:&lt;/strong&gt; No problem, thank you for answering my questions also, SCP-5913.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5913:&lt;/strong&gt; Yeah&amp;#8230;no problem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;[END LOG]&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
