					<![CDATA[
						 <div style="text-align: right;"></div> <p><strong>Item#:</strong> 5913</p> <p><strong>Object Class:</strong> <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">Euclid</span> Keter</p> <p><strong>Special Containment Procedures:</strong> Containment of SCP-5913 is a 16 x 60 ft (about 3.7 x 5.5m) room constructed out of tungsten. The subject is to keep under the observer of the foundation surveillances at all times. All personnel is to test for cognitohazardous corruption before they entered its containment cell. It was advised all personnel of the Foundation not to make any physical interactions with the subject.</p> <p><strong>Description</strong>: SCP-5913 is a humanoid entity dressed up in a bartender suit of the 1920s,<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-739877-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >1</a></sup> This may be either real cloth or some form of skin molded to take on cloth's appearance. Subject measures 6 to 15 feet tall have a general appearance as a tall black figure. Its face is pitch black, utterly devoid of facial features.<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-739877-2" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >2</a></sup></p> <p>The subject has no sign of hair, eyes, nose, and mouth can be opened up as an average human and has normal-looking bare hands, albeit with fingers longer and bonier than a typical human 1.5 meters each. However, it is possible that this is not SCP-5913's proper form and that it is an eldritch being that cannot comprehend whose proper form. It can speak and understand common human languages; however, the subject seems to have different respiratory sounds, which causes it to have issues in saying.</p> <p>Attempting to kill SCP-5913 often has some significant problems because of its considerable physical and uncommon abilities. It has always been observed to have chief strength, speed, and reflexes. The documented rate has varied; it can run with speed up to Mach 25; however, sometimes, the subject prefers to teleport rather than running.<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-739877-3" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >3</a></sup> Other than that, the subject is not sustainable. However, SCP-5913 has shown to have a remarkable ability to ignore pain, shock, and a decisive regenerate healing factor.<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-739877-4" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >4</a></sup></p> <p>The tendrils that sprout from SCP-5913's body can grab and attack; it can also use the tendrils as a shield to protect the entity away from harm.<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-739877-5" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >5</a></sup></p> <p>Its presence causes several adverse effects on the minds of its targets, including inhibiting memory loss, adding memory, altering sense and perception of a person's environment, influencing a person's personality in a very negative way such as causing a great deal of paranoia, nightmares, and hallucinations, Etc. It is believed that the presence of SCP-5913 directly causes adverse effects on the minds of whom it manifest. There is evidence that supports this belief. People who encounter it would become incredibly paranoid of its next return, easily irritated or agitated, severely depressed, and sometimes even suicidal. This method of negatively changing a person's personality could most likely result from its mind control.</p> <p>Documents of SCP-5913 anomalous abilities have shown particular individual contemporary views see its movement unlimited as if it can move its body properly. There is no apparent coherency to its positions. It can teleport several dozen times to various locations in a few seconds. SCP-5913 does not flee and can be just as dangerous standing still as when teleporting. It is capable of – and often will – stay within several dozen feet of its target, no matter how they try to escape. It seems to be part of SCP-5913's psychological ways of attacking to stay just within visual range without attacking — the fact that it is there, no matter what, it described worse than being attacked, the psychological effects often deteriorating the minds of its targets.</p> <p>SCP-5913 appears to follow all targets regardless of where they go or where and how they hide. It is not sure how it does this, but it seems to keep a perfect trace on its targets. These accounts vary from person to person, but being an SCP-5913 target is almost contagious or memetic. One can become its victim by encountering someone it is already targeting. Primary research and even collecting information does not appear to incur its notice. A theory sprouts from this, discussing how it could track several people at once due to the apparent number of people invested. This theory states he is an omnipresent being.</p> <p>Its skin can inflict diseases upon those who touch it; humans who come in contact with SCP-5913's skin would cause them to suffer some common ailments.<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-739877-6" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >6</a></sup></p> <hr /> <p><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>Addendum 5913.1: Discovery</strong></span></p> <p>In the mid-1900s, at the South East of America, the Foundation has written that following witness reports of something lurking inside a large abandoned row home located somewhere deep in the forest. These reports resulted in the dispatching of Mobile Task Force Omega-7, who arrived on site with 15 armed personnel. During capturing SCP-5913, seven (7) personnel were lost in action; however, later on, one of the agents had weakened a while later. After that, it got transported back to Site-19. However, due to having issues occur while traveling back, Omega-7 was ordered by the Foundation to transport SCP-5913 to Site-179, where it was contained in a reinforced 14m x 14m x 14m room made out of alloy steel. Armed guards are to be in place at all times to prevent unauthorized access to the facility. One of the foundation researchers, Dr.█████, interviewed it to see whether he can find anything to learn about SCP-5913.</p> <p><span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span></p> <div style="text-align: center;"> <div style="background: url(http://kaktuskontainer.wdfiles.com/local--files/format-hell/scp_trans.png) center no-repeat ; float: center; border: solid 2px #000000; padding: 1px 15px; box-shadow: 0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,.2);"> <h1><span>WARNING: THE FOLLOWING FILES ARE LEVEL 4/5913 CLASSIFIED</span></h1> <hr /> <h4><span>THE FOLLOWING FILES CONTAIN REFERENCES TO PROCEDURES RETROACTIVELY DECLARED BY THE ETHICS COMMITTEE TO BE RECKLESSLY NEGLIGENT. ANY FURTHER ATTEMPTS TO ACCESS MATERIALS RELATED TO THESE PROCEDURES WITHOUT PROPER CLEARANCE WILL LEAD TO IMMEDIATE DISCIPLINARY ACTION.</span></h4> </div> </div> <p><span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span></p> <hr /> <p><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>Addendum XXXX.1A: Interview and Experiment Logs</strong></span></p> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">SCP-5913-1A:&nbsp;Interview&nbsp;Log&nbsp;(10/10/1935)</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">ACCESS&nbsp;GRANTED</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <p><strong>Addendum 5913-1A Interview Log:</strong></p> <div style="display: inline-block; border-radius: 10px; border:dashed 1px #444444; background:#F5F5F5; float:top; width:96.5%; padding:10px"> <p><strong>[BEGIN LOG]</strong></p> <p><em>(SCP-5913 growls in an aggressive tone)</em></p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> Where am I?</p> <p><strong>Dr.█████:</strong> Calm down. We do not mean any harm to any at all.</p> <p><em>(Silence)</em></p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> &#8230;Who&#8230;are you? Furthermore, what do you want with me?</p> <p><strong>Dr.█████</strong> Yes, allow me to introduce myself; my Name is Dr.█████, and what I want is for you to answer some questions.</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> &#8230;What questions?</p> <p><strong>Dr.█████:</strong> It is nothing serious at all, I need to ask you a few simple questions, and that is all.</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> <em>(Silence)</em> Okay, I’m listening.</p> <p><strong>Dr.█████:</strong> So, first, may I know your name?</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> Name? I do not have a name.</p> <p><strong>Dr.█████:</strong> Is that so? In that case, would you mind if I refer to you as SCP-5913?</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> Well&#8230;if that is what you want to call me then, all right.</p> <p><strong>Dr.█████:</strong> Okay, so, what date were you born?</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> I also have no clue of what day, month, and the year I was born in.</p> <p><strong>Dr.█████:</strong> Okay, but I am still confused; earlier, we have sent a group of agents to come to your location. You have killed 7 of our agents before being weakened by the rest. If you can talk, then why didn't you tried to speak to field agents?</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> I thought they would not listen and would only kill me, so I have to fight back. I swear I do not want to kill or hurt anyone at all; it was just self-defense <em>(sighs)</em> I should have just teleported away.</p> <p><strong>Dr.█████:</strong> Wait, did you say you can teleport?</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> Yes, but I thought that if I let them live, they would lead back more and more &quot;agents&quot; to where I am from, and as I said from earlier, it was just self-defense. I did not want to die; that is all.</p> <p><strong>Dr.█████:</strong> all right, then how long have you been inside that abandoned row home?</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> To be honest, I cannot even possibly remember how long has I been in there, probably years perhaps&#8230;</p> <p><strong>Dr.█████:</strong> I see, however, if you cannot remember, or maybe do not have a name, and the date that you were born in, even how long you have been in that abandoned row home, then were you human once?</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> <em>(Silence)</em></p> <p><strong>Dr.█████:</strong> Uh, is everything all right?</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> Well, I do not recall any memories I have, but I still keep a few memories of my past-life before becoming like this.</p> <p><strong>Dr.█████:</strong> So you were once human, huh?</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> <em>(Nods)</em> Yes&#8230;however, I do not have the memories of my past-self, except for a little that I can still remember.</p> <p><strong>Dr.█████:</strong> Is that so?</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> Yeah&#8230;I-I can remember working as a bartender during the mid-1900s.</p> <p><strong>Dr.█████:</strong> Other than that, do you recall any other things else than your former job?</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> No, I think that is all I could remember…</p> <p><strong>Dr.█████:</strong> I see, so how do you feel now?</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> <em>(Silence)</em></p> <p><strong>Dr.█████:</strong> Um, excuse me, SCP-5913, are you listening?</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> <em>(Silence)</em></p> <p><strong>Dr.█████:</strong> SCP-XXXX, are you there?</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> <em>(Silence)</em> Oh! S-sorry about that, I was just being distracted, so what were you saying?</p> <p><strong>Dr.█████:</strong> Distracted? What exactly were you being distracted from?</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> <em>(Silence)</em> Is that even neccessary?</p> <p><strong>Dr.█████:</strong> Yes, it is. Everything related to you is necessary for the Foundation. So tell me, what were you being distracted from?</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> <em>(Sighs)</em> Well, I kind of sense vital energy flowing around this entire so-called &quot;facility&quot; it is compelling if you asked.</p> <p><strong>Dr.█████:</strong> What kind of compelling energy did you sense?</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> I do not know, but it makes me feel a bit of distress. This energy would be malevolence if you asked.</p> <p><strong>Dr.█████:</strong> I see, so where does this &quot;malevolence&quot; energy do you sense is coming from?</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> Well, I believed it is somewhere around this facility.</p> <p><strong>Dr.█████:</strong> I see. Is it possible that you were mentioning SCP-████</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong>, Huh? Who is that?</p> <p><strong>Dr.█████:</strong> Not important.</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> <em>(Silence)</em> Okay, but may I know why am I here in this place?</p> <p><strong>Dr.█████</strong> Well, to be fair, a few issues have occurred with one of our vehicles.</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> Oh, so it did work while I was still resting.</p> <p><strong>Dr.█████:</strong> Excuse me?</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> Well, moments ago, while I was resting inside the container to regain my strength, I think one of my powers must have caused some technological problems.</p> <p><strong>Dr.█████:</strong> Wait, so you tell me that you can cause out statics upon technology?</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> To be fair, I would prefer to call it a technological disruption. I had discovered that I could do so a few days earlier when I passed by a campsite, but I did not seem to get the hang of it yet heh.</p> <p><strong>Dr.█████:</strong> Wait, I am confused. How calm you used your anomalous abilities while resting?</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> You see here, my technological disruption does not work the way it was. It happens naturally, anywhere I go, it happens without I want it to.</p> <p><strong>Dr.█████:</strong> So you cannot control your powers, huh?</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> Yes, however, this power happens in random moments; it does not always happen, so I cannot tell when it will start to occur.</p> <p><strong>Dr.█████:</strong> Uh-huh, other than that, is there anything else that you want to share with me?</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> Well, so, am I going to be here, or what?</p> <p><strong>Dr.█████:</strong> You were supposed to be transported to a site that is far away from here. However, due to your powers interrupting the vehicle's control system, the Foundation has given out a new command was to temporarily transport you to this site until we received a new order from the Foundation.</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> <em>(Silence)</em> Which is?</p> <p><strong>Dr.█████:</strong> Well, of course, it is the order of the Foundation to transport you back to the site where you were supposed to be transferred to.</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> I see; thanks for informing me that.</p> <p><strong>Dr.█████:</strong> Okay, so how are you?</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> Excuse me? I did not quite get that. Can you be more specific about what you said just now?</p> <p><strong>Dr.█████:</strong> What is your impression of your time in the Foundation so far?</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> <em>(Silence)</em></p> <p><strong>Dr.█████:</strong> It is okay, to be honest. We do not take any offense at these things.</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> Well, this place&#8230;the so-called &quot;foundation&quot; seems to be like some prison or, to be specific, it is like a prison for peoples like me if I am not wrong. However, I know it is better than getting myself killed. However, I am also curious about what will happen to me after being transported to the other so-called &quot;site&quot;?</p> <p><strong>Dr.█████:</strong> Depends on the decisions of the Foundation, they will decide what to do with you.</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> <em>(Silence)</em> Okay, I get it&#8230;thanks for telling me this.</p> <p><strong>Dr.█████:</strong> No problem, thank you for answering my questions also, SCP-5913.</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> Yeah&#8230;no problem.</p> <p><strong>[END LOG]</strong></p> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">SCP-5913-L1</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">ACCESS&nbsp;GRANTED</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <div class="test"> <p><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>Experiment 5913-e-1:</strong></span></p> <p><strong>Name:</strong> Dr. Alex</p> <p><strong>Date:</strong> 08/16/1935</p> <p><strong>Procedure:</strong> A D-Class subject armed with an MP5 is to introduced inside the observation chamber with SCP-5913. SCP-5913 was asked to show its strange powers by Dr. Alex.</p> <p><strong>Results:</strong> SCP-5913 dodges the bullets without getting hit by any of them. It soon teleported in a blink of an eye and swiped its hand to destroy the MP5 that subject D-234532 is holding.</p> <p><strong>Afterword:</strong> SCP-XXXX was escorted back to its containment unit and asked how long it would need to test its anomalous abilities. They informed site staff that they should avoid SCP-5913 disturbances while resting inside its containment cell to SCP-5913's compliance.</p> <hr /> <blockquote> <p><strong>Note:</strong> Seems like it has some unchecked limitations. More testing to determine the boundaries of its anomaly will follow.</p> </blockquote> </div> <div class="test"> <p><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>Experiment 5913-e-2:</strong></span></p> <p><strong>Name:</strong> Dr. Alex with Dr. Claymore assisting</p> <p><strong>Date:</strong> 08/17/1935</p> <p><strong>Procedure:</strong> Another D-class subject is to be brought into the observation chamber with SCP-5913. SCP-5913 will instruct to make direct eye contact with the D-class subject.</p> <p><strong>Results:</strong> SCP-5913 stares at the D-class subject, Subject D-234536, but did not vocalize any concerns. Dr. Alex instructed SCP-5913 to comply with the request, and subject D-234536 was to make direct eye contact with it to see whether or not it is safe. Subject D-234536 made multiple explicit comments and was reminded of the consequence of unruly behavior. After 3 seconds later, Subject D-234536 reported that their eye-sight is beginning to see some statics, and just fainted. SCP-XXXX checks on the condition of the subject D-234536 as it became shocked and said that the D-class subject was dead.</p> <p><strong>Afterward:</strong> As SCP-5913 was being escorted back to its containment unit, it asked what will happen to it. The escort team ignored all questions.</p> <p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">-</span>-</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Note:</strong> It seems like SCP-5913 can cause out an instant death onto those who make eye contact with it longer than three (3) seconds.</p> </blockquote> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Access&nbsp;Incident&nbsp;Report:&nbsp;SCP-5913-1</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Retract&nbsp;Incident&nbsp;Report:&nbsp;SCP-XXXX-1</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <div style="float:center; display: block ; border : solid 2px #444444 ; background :#F5F5F5 ; width : 88% ; margin: 10px 10px 10px 10px; padding:1px 15px"> <p><strong>Foreword:</strong> The following incident report describes SCP-5913's technological disruption that has almost caused an event of containment breaches, which occurred during midnight after the experiment-5913-e-2.</p> <hr /> <p><strong>&lt;16:14&gt; -</strong> SCP-5913 was sleeping inside of its containment cell.</p> <p><strong>&lt;16:15&gt; -</strong> The surveillances of its containment chamber started to have some statics for a while before maintaining back naturally.</p> <p><strong>&lt;16:16&gt; -</strong> SCP-5913 begins to make slight movements with its arms during its sleep.</p> <p><strong>&lt;16:17&gt; -</strong> The surveillance suddenly got more statics but this time, it was longer and did not respond to any signal.</p> <p><strong>&lt;16:18&gt; -</strong> Sounds of SCP-5913's containment entrance door was heard opening during the statics.</p> <p><strong>&lt;16:19&gt;</strong> Alarm sounds were heard throughout the whole facility.</p> <p><strong>&lt;16:20&gt;</strong> The speaker begins to announce <em>&quot;Attention, all personnel, there seems to be a problem with the security system, the doors of all containment chambers of the facility seem to be having some issues incur, and are not responding to any of our attempts to close it, all personnel, report to [distortion]&#8230; &#8230;immediately.&quot; *Microphone cuts out*</em></p> <p><strong>&lt;16:21&gt;</strong> SCP-5913's voice was heard inside its containment <em>SCP-5913 &quot;*YAWN* huh? What is going on? Are we moving to? I did not remember having any scheduled.</em></p> <p><strong>&lt;16:22&gt;</strong> The surveillances of SCP-5913's containment chamber are maintained back generally as the entrance door of its containment chamber also closes.</p> <p><strong>&lt;16:23&gt;</strong> SCP-5913 looks around in confusion <em>SCP-SCP-5913: Huh? What just happened?</em></p> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Access&nbsp;Message&nbsp;from&nbsp;the&nbsp;O5-Council</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <div class="test"> <p>Dear Site-Director of Area-179,</p> <p>The order of O5-Council, SCP-5913, is to be transferred back to Site-19 and has to be moved into an enhanced containment unit. That being said, we have concluded that it would be beneficial for Site-19 as a whole to work to understand SCP-5913's capabilities better. Multiple options are being discussed, such as using it to assist in standard repairs and maintenance. However, specific influential individuals have also proposed using it to produce more valuable materials.</p> <p>All of this can only be accomplished if SCP-5913 is compliant with the Foundation procedures. All personnel assigned to interact with SCP-5913 directly have been sent a copy of the updated containment procedures and other relevant materials. Your mistake did not realize how versatile SCP-5913's anomaly was. Let us not make that mistake again.</p> <p><em>- O5-Council</em></p> </div> </div> </div> </div> <p><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>Addendum.5913.2: Transportation and interviewing log</strong></span><br /> On 08/20/1935, SCP-XXXX was transferred to Site-19, where it moved into an enhanced humanoid containment chamber. During the process of transportation, there were no signs of technology disruption occurring on the control system. SCP-XXXX did not show out any signs of attempted to escape nor hostile. After transportation, SCP-XXXX has another interview session with Dr.Warren.</p> <p><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>Addendum 5913.2A: Interview and Experiment Logs</strong></span></p> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">SCP-XXXX-2B:&nbsp;Interview&nbsp;Log&nbsp;(10/10/1935)</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">ACCESS&nbsp;GRANTED</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <p><strong>Addendum 5913-2B Interview Log:</strong></p> <div style="display: inline-block; border-radius: 10px; border:dashed 1px #444444; background:#F5F5F5; float:top; width:96.5%; padding:10px"> <p><strong>[BEGIN LOG]</strong></p> <p><strong>Dr. Warren:</strong> Hello there, SCP-5913.</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> Yes, hello.</p> <p><strong>Dr. Warren:</strong> Allow me to introduce myself, my name is Dr.Warren, and I have conducted another interview session with you.</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> Wait, does every one of these so-called &quot;SCP&quot; always have an interview with a doctor when they get transport to another place?</p> <p><strong>Dr. Warren:</strong> <em>(Silence)</em> That I cannot tell. However, right now, we just need to learn more about you, and that is all.</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> <em>(Silence)</em> Okay, I am listening to whatever questions your about to ask me.</p> <p><strong>Dr. Warren:</strong> Yes, so according to the reports we have received from Site-179, you have caused some significant issues over there.</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> Wait, what?</p> <p><strong>Dr. Warren:</strong> I see that they have not told you everything about the incident that has occurred. Last night, your so-called technological disruption caused several malfunctioning issues with the facility's security system, almost causing a containment breach event.</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> Oh, is that good or bad?</p> <p><strong>Dr. Warren:</strong> It is bad SCP-5913.</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> Oh, man. This isn't good.</p> <p><strong>Dr. Warren:</strong> Indeed, because of &quot;that&quot; incident that happens last night caused by you, the Foundation decided to move you here as soon as possible to learn more about you and your powers, and hopefully, we could find a solution to prevent it from happening again.</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> I see. I hope that my powers did not cause out any influences upon the Foundation.</p> <p><strong>Dr. Warren:</strong> Yes, you should be. However, I have also received reports about you mentioning malevolence energy flowing inside Site-179, and reports of Dr.█████ that you must have possibly sent that malevolence energy coming from SCP-████.</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> Yeah, but I am curious, of whoever is this SCP-████, can you tell me about that SCP?</p> <p><strong>Dr. Warren:</strong> I am afraid that that kind of information cannot be revealed to anyone at all, even someone like you, SCP-XXXX.</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> <em>(Silence)</em> All right, but I am still curious about that SCP.</p> <p><strong>Dr. Warren:</strong> Okay, now, do you still sense that malevolence energy?</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> Wait! You said that that SCP is not important at all.</p> <p><strong>Dr. Warren:</strong> When I said that it has nothing to do with you, I meant its information has nothing to do with you; we are still talking about that malevolence energy you have sensed from Site-179. It is just not the necessary information about SCP-████ only.</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> Okay, so what are the questions?</p> <p><strong>Dr. Warren:</strong> It is simple. Do you still feel that &quot;malevolence&quot; energy?</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> <em>(Silence)</em> Well, no, but there seem to be a few dark energy flowing in this facility, except that it is not intensely strong as that energy I sent yesterday back at the so-called &quot;Site-179.&quot;. However, I have also sent a few benevolence energy in this facility, well, less benevolence energy if you asked.</p> <p><strong>Dr. Warren:</strong> I see, so, how do you feel after being away from that malevolence energy?</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> Well, I felt less distress. However, I kept on sensing the malevolence energy during my time in that place, keeping on growing bigger and bigger, like something very evil.</p> <p><strong>Dr.Warren:</strong> Okay, I see. Thank you for answering my questions.</p> <p><strong>SCP-5913:</strong> Yeah, no worries, I'm getting used to having these interviews.</p> <p><strong>[END LOG]</strong></p> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">SCP-5913-L2</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">ACCESS&nbsp;GRANTED</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <div class="test"> <p><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>Experiment 5913-e-3:</strong></span></p> <p><strong>Name:</strong> Dr. Emorden</p> <p><strong>Date:</strong> 08/20/1935</p> <p><strong>Procedure:</strong> SCP-5913 was told to demonstrate its teleportation abilities in the observation chamber of Site-19, and a D-Class subject, D-59103, was told to observe SCP-5913 to see whether if any paranormal effects occur during the process of its teleportation.</p> <p><strong>Results:</strong> SCP-5913 made its attempts in teleporting. Subject D-59103 reported that he sees nothing but just statics in a short period before regaining their eye-sights back normally. Dr. Emorden instructed the subject D-59103 to keep on observing SCP-5913 and told SCP-5913 to teleport once more. Subject D-59103 reported that they still see nothing but just statics.</p> <p><strong>Afterword:</strong> SCP-5913 was escorted back to its containment unit without saying anything to the escorted team.</p> <hr /> <blockquote> <p><strong>Note:</strong> It seems like SCP-5913 has some sort of anomalous effects that seems to blind the eye-sight of those who are looking at it during the process of its teleportation. However, it was yet confirmed whether these effects were used to overwhelm those who look at it, or SCP-XXXX may have some sort of passive modification that allows it to warp space and time. And the statics reported by subject D-59103 from earlier was one of its effects. More tests to determine the boundaries of its anomaly will follow.</p> </blockquote> <p><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>Experiment 5913-e-4:</strong></span></p> <p><strong>Name:</strong> Dr. Emorden with Dr. Taylor assisting</p> <p><strong>Date:</strong> 08/21/1935</p> <p><strong>Procedure:</strong> Dr. Emorden instructed SCP-5913 to demonstrate whether it really has the modification to warp space and time on a D-Class subject, D-605913, that has been introduced inside of the observation chamber along with a pen.</p> <p><strong>Results:</strong> It proceeded to raised out its hand. Subject D-605913 begins to see their body being glitched. Subject screams in agony before being turned into a picture. The photograph contains the subject D-605913, who is shouting and demanding SCP-5913 to let them out.</p> <p><strong>Afterword:</strong> SCP-5913 soon turned the picture back to the subject D-605913 normally and was escorted back to its containment unit. SCP-5913 asked what is going to happen with it now. All questions were ignored once again by the escort team.</p> <hr /> <blockquote> <p><strong>Note:</strong> It would appear that SCP-5913 has a substantial modification to warp not just space and time but even a fraction of reality itself. However, it is possible that this is not the only effect that it could cause, as if it is shown to have the potentials to cause out serious disturbances towards the balance of space and time, or possibly reality. And with SCP-5913's condition from earlier, it would appear like that it has no sympathy for bad humans, as it was able to sense the malevolence inside of them also.</p> </blockquote> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class="footnotes-footer"> <div class="title">Footnotes</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-739877-1"><a href="javascript:;" >1</a>. Which comprised wearing a white shirt, a black or red tie, black trousers, and black shoes.</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-739877-2"><a href="javascript:;" >2</a>. Despite lacking facial features, SCP-5913 can sense when its targets are near at all times, as it never hesitates and always sees the marks around it</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-739877-3"><a href="javascript:;" >3</a>. Its teleportation is also described as a phenomenon which is a term of SCP-5913's apparent teleportation, or perhaps it is using some passive modification to warp space and time. These abilities were seen as one of the most recognizable elements ability to appear – seemingly from nowhere – in a place where it was not mere seconds. These were one of its traits and mentioned the effect of this on a person's mental health.</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-739877-4"><a href="javascript:;" >4</a>. Prior encounters have shown that SCP-5913 capable of: <ul> <li>Rip through a wall made of steel with the course of using only two of its hands.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>Dodging various bullets without showing out signs of being tired.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>Teleporting to various locations.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>A single swipe of its hand destroys an assault rifle.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>Changing its height and body shape.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>Sprouting out tendrils from all over its entire body.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>SCP-5913 potentially can choose who sees it and when in many cases. For instance, SCP-5913 can allow only one person to see it, or only the target, but not anyone. However, it is commonly agreed that even when humans can not detect it, it is still visible at cameras, both digital and pre-digital. However, there is often distortion when captured digitally.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>SCP-5913 can cause out technological disruption naturally. This happens at random times.</li> </ul> </div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-739877-5"><a href="javascript:;" >5</a>. So far, the subject's tendrils shown to have: <ul> <li>Blocking gunshots and melee weapons.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>Move with speed faster than the blink of an eye.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>Able to stretch for an extensive range of distance.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>Able to withstand the powerful explosions from grenades, and sometimes it can even be sustainable against a missile. However, it depends on how much strength the subject still has left inside of it.</li> </ul> </div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-739877-6"><a href="javascript:;" >6</a>. Diseases the skin of SCP-5913 has applied to those who touch it: <ul> <li>Ischemic heart disease.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>Lower respiratory infections.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>Stroke diseases.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>Cerebrovascular diseases.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>Alzheimer's disease and other dementias.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>Diabetes mellitus.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>Trachea, bronchus, and lung cancers.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>Tuberculosis</li> </ul> </div> </div> <p>by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/godlyuser" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6876114&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606983581" alt="GodlyUser" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6876114)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/godlyuser" >GodlyUser</a></span></p> 
