					<![CDATA[
						 <div style="display: none"></div> <div style="text-align: right;"></div> <div style="text-align: center;"><img src="http://www.scp-wiki.net/local--files/the-graveyard/memoriabanner.jpg" alt="memoriabanner.jpg" class="image" /><br /> <span style="font-family: 'Nanum Brush Script', cursive; color: #390000;font-size: 450%;">In Memoria, Malyce</span></div> <div class="type1"> <p><sup>1</sup>And it came to pass in those days that there was a great lamentation, for Malyce Graves had died.<br /> <sup>2</sup>Lo, even after death, the frantic scribblings continued unabated, and word after word spilled forth from the gaping maw of that unholy sepulcher. Scribbles like many had yet seen, though few believed.<br /> <sup>3</sup> For, in their heart of hearts, the readers knew that these words were the ravings of a broken, yet cunningly demented mind.<br /></p> <div style="text-align: right;"> <p><span style="font-family:var(--body-font); font-size: calc(var(--base-font-size) * 1.00); color: #000000;">- <em>The Unquiet Grave</em>, An autobiography</span></p> </div> </div> <hr /> <div class="addenda-header"> <h3><span><span style="font-family: 'Nanum Brush Script', cursive; color: #390000; font-size: 150%"><strong>A Insania in Auditorio</strong></span></span></h3> </div> <br /> <div id="wiki-tabview-c2ef1c93880ad789cd81518f2464c6bc" class="yui-navset"> <ul class="yui-nav"> <li class="selected"><a href="javascript:;"><em>Raving</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>In Memoria</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>Commendatur lectio</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>Verbum est Perpetua</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>Ars ab aliis</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>Lectio instrumentum ad</em></a></li> </ul> <div class="yui-content"> <div id="wiki-tab-0-0"> <h4><span><span style="font-family: 'Nanum Brush Script', cursive; color: #390000; font-size: 150%">Tales -</span></span></h4> <table style="width: 100%; border-spacing: 0; border-collapse: collapse;"> <tr> <td style="text-align: left; width: 100%;"><span style="font-family: 'Nanum Brush Script', cursive; color: #390000; font-size: 150%"><strong>I &lt;3 the Circus</strong></span></td> </tr> <tr> <td style="text-align: Left; width: 40%;"> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/a-night-at-the-circus">Pt.1 - A Night at the Circus</a> - Wherein our Protagonist finds themselves at the Circus</li> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/amongst-the-clowns">Pt.2 - Amongst the Clowns</a> - Wherein our Protagonist is captured by Clowns</li> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/i-heart-the-circus-3">Pt. &lt;3 - Wherever You Go, I'll Follow</a> - Wherein our Protagonist falls in love</li> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/i-heart-the-circus-4">Pt. 4 - For Fear of Falling</a> - Wherein our Protagonist learns to fly</li> </ul> </td> </tr> <tr> <td style="text-align: left; width: 100%;"><span style="font-family: 'Nanum Brush Script', cursive; color: #390000; font-size: 150%"><strong>Other Tales</strong></span></td> </tr> <tr> <td style="text-align: left; width: 1000%;"> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/the-machine">The Sisyphean Machine</a> - Wherein our Protagonist is forever lost</li> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/anthropological-report-darkwater">Case Study 03: The Darkwater Lodge</a> - Wherein our Protagonist learns about a Neo-Sarkic cult</li> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/midnight-neon">Midnight in the Neon City</a> - Wherein our Protagonist gets mugged</li> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/swamplight">s w a m p l i g h t</a> - Wherein our Protagonist isn't who we think he is ||</li> <li><a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/lovataar-throne">Of Lovataar &amp; the Throne</a> - Wherein our Protagonist suffers for love</li> <li><a href="http://scpwiki.com/kelipat">Kelipat Nogah</a> - Wherein our Protagonist issues a call to action</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/patience">Patience</a> - Wherein our Protagonist laments their lack of understanding.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/unbearable-hope">Unbearable Hope</a> - Wherein our Protagonist endures the price of hope</li> </ul> </td> </tr> <tr> <td style="text-align: left; width: 100%;"><span style="font-family: 'Nanum Brush Script', cursive; color: #390000; font-size: 150%"><strong>Written Elsewhere</strong></span></td> </tr> <tr> <td style="border-bottom: 1px solid #000; text-align: left; width: 1000%;"> <ul> <li><a href="http://wanderers-library.wikidot.com/homeland">Homeland</a> - Found in the <a href="http://wanderers-library.wikidot.com/">Wanderer's Library</a></li> </ul> </td> </tr> </table> <h4><span><span style="font-family: 'Nanum Brush Script', cursive; color: #390000; font-size: 150%">Set Pieces -</span></span></h4> <table style="width: 100%; border-spacing: 0; border-collapse: collapse;"> <tr> <td style="text-align: left; width: 100%;"><span style="font-family: 'Nanum Brush Script', cursive; color: #390000; font-size: 150%"><strong>SCPF Documentation</strong></span></td> </tr> <tr> <td style="text-align: left; width: 40%;"> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-4459">SCP-4459: The Ringmaster's Crown</a> - Where we learn of love that lasts</li> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-4476">SCP-4476: La Famille Natau</a> - Where we learn about a family in a swamp</li> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-4421">SCP-4421: Papa Legba's Walkin' Stick</a> - Where we learn of an Old God and His walkin' stick</li> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-5501">SCP-5501: Empty Portraits</a> - Where we learn about madness, cameras, and war</li> <li><a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/scp-3862">SCP-3862: The Gentleman Karcist</a> - Where we learn about the love of a Karcist</li> <li><a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/scp-3385">SCP-3385: The Last Voyage of the Far Horizon</a> - Where we find out about the death of hope</li> <li><a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/scp-3911">SCP-3911: The Thorn of God</a> - Where we learn that some gods should stay dead</li> <li><a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/scp-4786">SCP-4786: The Mouth that Hungers</a> - Where we learn about Sarkic flesh dolls</li> <li><a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/scp-2834">SCP-2834: The Blood of MEKHANE</a> - Where we see the price of hubris</li> </ul> </td> </tr> <tr> <td style="text-align: left; width: 100%;"><span style="font-family: 'Nanum Brush Script', cursive; color: #390000; font-size: 150%"><strong>GoI Formats</strong></span></td> </tr> <tr> <td style="border-bottom: 1px solid #000; text-align: left; width: 100%;"> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/the-penitent-man">HF Presents: The Penitent Man</a> - Where we learn about one of the Performers at the Circus of the Disquieting</li> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/nancy-shoe">LaRue Post - Nancy's Shoe</a> - Where we find out why Nancy's not a salesman</li> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/larue-post-bang">LaRue Post - BANG!</a> - Where we find Scratch trying to sell a &quot;firework&quot;</li> </ul> </td> </tr> </table> <h4><span><span style="font-family: 'Nanum Brush Script', cursive; color: #390000; font-size: 150%">Collaborations -</span></span></h4> <table style="width: 100%; border-spacing: 0; border-collapse: collapse;"> <tr> <td style="border-bottom: 1px solid #000; text-align: left; width: 50%;"> <p>With <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/plaidypus" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4187161&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606983586" alt="plaidypus" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4187161)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/plaidypus" >plaidypus</a></span>:</p> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-5335">SCP-5335: The Freudian Split</a></li> <li><a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/scp-5038">SCP-5038: La Rue Macabre is CLOSED</a></li> </ul> <p>With <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/drakimoto" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5255688&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606983586" alt="DrAkimoto" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5255688)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/drakimoto" >DrAkimoto</a></span>:</p> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/ulysses-b-donkman-and-the-clockwork-bandits">Donkman &amp; The Clockwork Bandits</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/ulysses-b-donkman-and-the-mournful-birthday">Donkman &amp; The Mournful Birthday</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/ulysses-b-donkman-and-the-foreboding-forest">Donkman &amp; The Foreboding Forest, Pt.1</a></li> <li><a href="http://scpwiki.com/ulysses-b-donkman-and-the-foreboding-forest2">Donkman &amp; The Foreboding Forest, Pt. 2</a></li> <li><a href="http://scp-wiki.net/scp-5108">SCP-5108: We See You</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-5207">SCP-5207: Fit for the King</a></li> <li><a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/scp-4639">SCP-4639: Product Profile - Citrus Vitae</a></li> <li><a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/manufactured-nostalgia">Manufactured Nostalgia</a></li> <li><a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/scp-5506">SCP-5506: The Best Part Of Waking Up Is Manifesting a New God</a><sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-359281-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >1</a></sup></li> </ul> <p>With <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/cybersqyd" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5336470&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606983586" alt="cybersqyd" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5336470)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/cybersqyd" >cybersqyd</a></span>:</p> <ul> <li><a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/scp-5862">SCP-5862: Faulkner's Wake</a></li> <li><a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/regarding-scp-5862">SCP-5862 Historical Documentation</a></li> </ul> </td> <td style="border-bottom: 1px solid #000; text-align: left; width: 50%;"> <p>With <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dyslexion" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5549954&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606983586" alt="Dyslexion" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5549954)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dyslexion" >Dyslexion</a></span>:</p> <ul> <li><a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/scp-5573">SCP-5573: The Eyes of Heaven</a></li> </ul> <p>With <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/drhawkwind" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=993076&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606983586" alt="DrHawkwind" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=993076)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/drhawkwind" >DrHawkwind</a></span>:</p> <ul> <li><a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/scp-4764">SCP-4764: OKKULT X-PERIENCE OF WYRLDENDING PORPORTIONS</a> - (corpsecon entry)</li> </ul> <p>With <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/n-aepic-fael" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4463776&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606983586" alt="N_Aepic_Fael" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4463776)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/n-aepic-fael" >N_Aepic_Fael</a></span>:</p> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/et-ecce">Et Ecce Equus Pallidus</a> -</li> </ul> <p>With <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/mew-ltiverse" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5271378&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606983586" alt="Mew-ltiverse" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5271378)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/mew-ltiverse" >Mew-ltiverse</a></span>:</p> <ul> <li><a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/scp-5071">SCP-5071: Exquisite Corpses</a> -</li> </ul> <p>With <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/twistedfox" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6797425&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606983586" alt="TwistedFox" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6797425)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/twistedfox" >TwistedFox</a></span>:</p> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/i-heart-the-circus-4">Pt. 4 - For Fear of Falling</a></li> </ul> </td> </tr> </table> <h4><span><span style="font-family: 'Nanum Brush Script', cursive; color: #390000; font-size: 150%">Hubs, Guides, and Essays -</span><sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-359281-2" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >2</a></sup></span></h4> <table style="width: 100%; border-spacing: 0; border-collapse: collapse;"> <tr> <td style="text-align: left; width: 100%;"><span style="font-family: 'Nanum Brush Script', cursive; color: #390000; font-size: 150%"><strong>Hubs</strong></span></td> </tr> <tr> <td style="text-align: left; width: 100%;"> <ul> <li><a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/memoria-adytum">In Memoria, Adytum</a> - Grand Karcist Ion always knew he had to fall.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/larue-hub">La Rue Macabre Hub</a> - Down in the swamp, anything can happen</li> <li><a href="http://scp-wiki.net/the-donkman-s-den">The Donkman's Den</a> - Some stories just seem unreal even before they're told</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/guide-hub">Guide Hub</a> - Re-written in collaboration with <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/themightymcb" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4483018&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606983586" alt="TheMightyMcB" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4483018)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/themightymcb" >TheMightyMcB</a></span></li> </ul> </td> </tr> <tr> <td style="text-align: left; width: 100%;"><span style="font-family: 'Nanum Brush Script', cursive; color: #390000; font-size: 150%"><strong>Guides &amp; Essays</strong></span></td> </tr> <tr> <td style="border-bottom: 1px solid #000; text-align: left; width: 100%;"> <ul> <li><a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/avoid-the-blackbox">What Hides Beneath: the Black and White of Blackboxing</a> - SCP-Wiki Guide to Redaction</li> </ul> </td> </tr> </table> <h4><span><span style="font-family: 'Nanum Brush Script', cursive; color: #390000; font-size: 150%">Translations -</span></span></h4> <table style="width: 100%; border-spacing: 0; border-collapse: collapse;"> <tr> <td style="text-align: left; width: 100%;"> <p><span style="font-family: 'Nanum Brush Script', cursive; color: #390000; font-size: 150%"><strong>Korean -</strong></span></p> <ul> <li><a href="http://ko.scp-wiki.net/larue-hub">라 뤼 마카브르 허브</a> - La Rue Hub</li> <li><a href="http://ko.scp-wiki.net/theme:laruetheme">라 뤼 마카브르 테마</a> La Rue Theme</li> <li><a href="http://ko.scp-wiki.net/anthropological-report-darkwater">사르킥교의 인류학적 접근 - 사례연구 03: 어둔물 별장</a> - Darkwater Report</li> <li><a href="http://ko.scp-wiki.net/memoria-adytum">[인 메모리아 아뒤툼</a> Memoria, Adytum Hub</li> </ul> <p><span style="font-family: 'Nanum Brush Script', cursive; color: #390000; font-size: 150%"><strong>Japanese -</strong></span></p> <ul> <li><a href="http://scp-jp.wikidot.com/larue-hub">ラ・リュー・マカーブラー ハブ</a> - La Rue Hub</li> <li><a href="http://scp-jp.wikidot.com/scp-4764">SCP-4764</a></li> <li><a href="http://scp-jp.wikidot.com/manufactured-nostalgia">製造された郷愁</a> - Manufactured Nostalgia</li> <li><a href="http://scp-jp.wikidot.com/scp-3862">SCP-3862</a></li> <li><a href="http://scp-jp.wikidot.com/lovataar-throne">ロヴァタールと玉座</a> - Of Lovataar &amp; the Throne</li> <li><a href="http://scp-jp.wikidot.com/anthropological-report-darkwater">サーキシズムへの人類学的アプローチ──ケーススタディ03: 黒き水のロッジ</a> - Darkwater Report</li> <li><a href="http://scp-jp.wikidot.com/et-ecce">第一幕: 見よ、蒼ざめたる馬来たりて</a> - Et Ecce Equus Pallidus</li> <li><a href="http://scp-jp.wikidot.com/memoria-adytum">追憶のアディトゥム</a> - Memoria, Adytum Hub</li> <li><a href="http://scp-jp.wikidot.com/the-donkman-s-den">ドンクマンのアジト ハブ</a> Donkman's Den Hub</li> </ul> <p><span style="font-family: 'Nanum Brush Script', cursive; color: #390000; font-size: 150%"><strong>Spanish -</strong></span></p> <ul> <li><a href="http://lafundacionscp.wikidot.com/avoid-the-blackbox">El {CENSURADO} de la ██</a> - Redaction Guide</li> <li><a href="http://lafundacionscp.wikidot.com/lovataar-throne">De Lovataar y el Trono</a> - Of Lovataar &amp; the Throne</li> <li><a href="http://lafundacionscp.wikidot.com/scp-3862">SCP-3862</a></li> <li><a href="http://lafundacionscp.wikidot.com/scp-4786">SCP-4786</a></li> <li><a href="http://lafundacionscp.wikidot.com/anthropological-report-darkwater">Un Acercamiento Antropológico al Sarkicismo - Caso de Estudio 03: La Logia Aguasnegras</a> - Darkwater Report</li> <li><a href="http://lafundacionscp.wikidot.com/memoria-adytum">En Memoria, Adytum</a></li> </ul> <p><span style="font-family: 'Nanum Brush Script', cursive; color: #390000; font-size: 150%"><strong>Chinese -</strong></span></p> <ul> <li><a href="http://scp-wiki-cn.wikidot.com/nancy-shoe">LaRue 海報 - 南希的鞋子</a> - Nancy's Shoe</li> <li><a href="http://scp-wiki-cn.wikidot.com/larue-post-bang">LaRue 海報 - 砰!</a> BANG!</li> <li><a href="http://scp-wiki-cn.wikidot.com/scp-4786">SCP-4786</a></li> <li><a href="http://scp-wiki-cn.wikidot.com/lovataar-throne">拉娃塔与御座</a> - Of Lovataar &amp; the Throne</li> <li><a href="http://scp-wiki-cn.wikidot.com/memoria-adytum">追忆，内殿</a> - Memoria, Adytum Hub</li> <li><a href="http://scp-wiki-cn.wikidot.com/larue-hub">骇灵街</a> - La Rue Macabre Hub</li> <li><a href="http://scp-wiki-cn.wikidot.com/the-donkman-s-den">驴哥的窝点 中心页</a> - Donkman's Den Hub</li> <li><a href="http://scp-wiki-cn.wikidot.com/midnight-neon">子夜霓都</a> - Midnight in the Neon City</li> </ul> <p><span style="font-family: 'Nanum Brush Script', cursive; color: #390000; font-size: 150%"><strong>Russian -</strong></span></p> <ul> <li><a href="http://scpfoundation.net/scp-3911">SCP-3911 - Шип бога</a></li> <li><a href="http://scpfoundation.net/lovataar-throne">О Ловатаар и Троне</a> - Of Lovataar &amp; the Throne</li> <li><a href="http://scpfoundation.net/anthropological-report-darkwater">Антропологический подход к саркицизму — Социологический портрет 03: Ложа Тёмных Вод</a> - Darkwater Report</li> <li><a href="http://scpfoundation.net/the-machine">Сизифова Машина</a> - The Sisyphean Machine</li> <li><a href="http://scpfoundation.net/scp-5862">SCP-5862 - След корабля Фолкнера</a></li> <li><a href="http://scpfoundation.net/regarding-scp-5862">SCP-5862 - След корабля Фолкнера » Об SCP-5862</a></li> <li><a href="http://scpfoundation.net/scp-2834">SCP-2834 Кровь МЕХАН</a></li> </ul> <p><span style="font-family: 'Nanum Brush Script', cursive; color: #390000; font-size: 150%"><strong>French -</strong></span></p> <ul> <li><a href="http://fondationscp.wikidot.com/scp-5501">SCP-5501</a></li> </ul> <p><span style="font-family: 'Nanum Brush Script', cursive; color: #390000; font-size: 150%"><strong>Traditional Chinese -</strong></span></p> <ul> <li><a href="http://scp-zh-tr.wikidot.com/nancy-shoe">LaRue 海報 - 南希的鞋子</a> - Nancy's Shoe</li> <li><a href="http://scp-zh-tr.wikidot.com/larue-post-bang">LaRue 海報 - 砰!</a> - Bang!</li> </ul> </td> </tr> </table> </div> <div id="wiki-tab-0-1" style="display:none"> <h4><span><span style="font-family: 'Nanum Brush Script', cursive; color: #390000; font-size: 150%">I &lt;3 the Circus</span></span></h4> <p>This tale series is the introduction of a few new Circus characters. While it isn't explicit throughout the story (so far), the Protagonist eventually attains the name Cahaya. The relationship between Cahaya and Fraust is really the first thing I've added to the site, and I'm quite glad that the first thing I put in is a love story. It starts with the I &lt;3 the Circus, and then ends with <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-4459">SCP-4459: The Ringmaster's Crown</a>. Time is funky, because in my headcanon, the Kaleidoscope allows for opening Ways into the past.</p> <p>Some of the feedback I've gotten has been about how forced the gender stuff appears. Cahaya is meant to be whatever gender you assign to them. I wanted it to be very fluid on that. Also, Fraust is a Clown, and can change their gender at will. Sooo, yeah. Gender fluidity is deeply personal to me, and I wanted to showcase that in my stories about these people.</p> <p>I'd like to dedicate all of these stories to my beloved boyfriend. He's an acrobat/contortionist/aerialist in the real-world circus, and my love for him is intermixed with my love of Herman Fuller's Circus. Thank you for being such a light in my life, and for your unfailing love and support. You give me the strength to continue, to be better, to be worthy. &lt;3</p> <h4><span><span style="font-family: 'Nanum Brush Script', cursive; color: #390000; font-size: 150%">SCP-5501: Empty Portraits</span></span></h4> <p>This represents a significant amount of research into the American Civil War as well as the impact of that conflict upon the mental health of the people that participated. As one of the bloodiest periods of my nation's history, the impact of that war has etched itself deeply upon the collective psyche of the people that survived it and the descendants.</p> <p>I am a first generation American. Both sides of my parental lineage stretch far back through centuries of conflict and death, so while I cannot say that the echoes of the American Civil War still ring in my blood, I see the horrors of my own cultural legacy mirrored in it.</p> <p>While I am excited to write fiction about these events, I think it is tremendously important to keep in mind that these events happened. There is no horror that I can craft in the comfort of my office chair that will ever match the horror experienced by the people that fought and died in that war, or any war. Out of respect, I have kept as close to the source material as possible.</p> <p>All of the officers mentioned here are real people. The battles and dates of the battles mentioned here are real. The only one that wasn't is &quot;Massacre at Seven Pines&quot;, that is entirely of my creation. The horror of The Battle of The Crater is real, and the racism that added to that needless slaughter was also real.</p> <p>Let us not forget that this war was fought, and a great many people died, for the &quot;right&quot; of the Southern States to own slaves. This horrific stain on my Nation's history must never be forgotten lest we become complacent, and thus complicit, in the practice of trafficking and sale of human beings all around the globe.</p> </div> <div id="wiki-tab-0-2" style="display:none"> <p>Here are some Authors I think you should check out:</p> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/hammermaidens-author-page">HammerMaiden</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/themightymcb-s-author-page">TheMightyMcB</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/doctor-s-s-personnel-file">SoullessSingularity</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/dr-john-peppersghost-pepper-s-personnel-file">PeppersGhost</a></li> <li><a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/manymeats">ManyMeats</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.wikidot.com/drakimoto-s-author-page">DrAkimoto</a></li> </ul> <hr /> <p>My favorites:</p> <ul> <li><a href="http://scp-wiki.net/scp-4140">SCP-4140: Sarkic Containment Procedures</a></li> <li><a href="http://scp-wiki.net/scp-2000">SCP-2000: Deus Ex Machina</a></li> <li><a href="http://scp-wiki.net/scp-4203">SCP-4203: Sometimes a Damselfly Just Wants Some Dick</a></li> <li><a href="http://scp-wiki.net/scp-2264">SCP-2264: In the Court of Alagadda</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-1921">SCP-1921: Black Cotton Candy</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-1921">SCP-4840: The Demon Lancelot and the Flying City of Audapaupadopolis</a></li> <li><a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/scp-5805">SCP-5805: You Can't Go Back</a></li> <li><a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/the-foundation-eats-babies">Tales of the Ethics Committee: The Foundation Eats Babies</a></li> </ul> <hr /></div> <div id="wiki-tab-0-3" style="display:none"> <h3><span><span style="font-family: 'Nanum Brush Script', cursive; color: #390000; font-size: 150%">If I am Gone</span></span></h3> <p>In the event that I have disappeared off of the wiki and IRC for a period longer than 6 months without any notice or updates, I entrust the curation of all my solo <em>La Rue Macabre</em> content to <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/plaidypus" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4187161&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606983586" alt="plaidypus" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4187161)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/plaidypus" >plaidypus</a></span>, all my other solo stuff to <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/drakimoto" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5255688&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606983586" alt="DrAkimoto" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5255688)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/drakimoto" >DrAkimoto</a></span>, and my collaborative articles with their respective co-authors.</p> <p>These curators are expressly allowed to make substantive modifications to my work, provided it doesn't change the overall theme of the piece. (An Alagaddan skip will remain Alaggadan, etc.)</p> <h4><span><span style="font-family: 'Nanum Brush Script', cursive; color: #390000; font-size: 150%">If Anybody Needs Me</span></span></h4> <p>In the event that somebody on the wiki needs me and I am not responding to Wikidot PMs or IRC, <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/soullesssingularity" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=637830&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606983586" alt="SoullessSingularity" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=637830)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/soullesssingularity" >SoullessSingularity</a></span> has my personal cell number and can communicate with me offline.</p> </div> <div id="wiki-tab-0-4" style="display:none"> <div style="text-align: center;"> <p><span style="font-size:135%;"><strong>All my artwork can be found at <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/the-graveyard">The Graveyard</a></strong></span></p> </div> <hr /> <h3><span>From <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/barredowl" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6001754&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606983586" alt="barredowl" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6001754)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/barredowl" >barredowl</a></span>:</span></h3> <h3><span>Because I am a practicing Sar-kick.</span></h3> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Show&nbsp;image</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide&nbsp;image</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <div style="border: 1px solid #000;"> <div style="height: 100%;"> <div class="image-container aligncenter"><img src="http://scp-wiki.wdfiles.com/local--files/malycegraves-author/frombar